{
  "id": "PPA-06",
  "title": "Lipid Metabolism & Membrane Dynamics",
  "subtitle": "Plastid de novo fatty acid synthesis, ER eukaryotic Kennedy pathway, and peroxisomal beta-oxidation",
  "caption": "Integrated lipid biosynthesis, membrane remodeling, and turnover. De novo 16:0 and 18:0 fatty acids are synthesized by heteromeric ACCase and the FAS complex in plastids, followed by thioesterase hydrolysis (FATB/FATA). Free fatty acids export to the endoplasmic reticulum for incorporation into triacylglycerols (TAG storage) and structural galactolipids (MGDG/DGDG) by MGD1 and DGD1. Surplus or mobilizing lipids undergo peroxisomal beta-oxidation (ACX, MFP2, PED1/KAT2).",
  "species_anchor": "arabidopsis_thaliana",
